WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.880
You probably know The Beatles White Album,
and Jay-Z’s Black Album.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.520
But do you remember the Grey Album?

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.469
In 2004, the producer Danger Mouse combined
the vocals of The Black Album with samples

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:18.880
from the White album to create a mash-up of
the two…

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.830
This isn’t the only time that the world’s
best-selling band has collided with Hip Hop

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:23.830
and r&amp;b.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:33.040
Back in 1987, KRS-One interpolated the melody
from Hey Jude, on the song Criminal Minded.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.180
In the Wu-Tang song “The Heart Gently Weeps”
they got George Harrison’s son Dhani to

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:44.020
recreate his dad’s guitar riff.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.090
More recently, Frank Ocean thanked the Beatles
for single-handedly getting him out of his

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.190
writer’s block.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.749
He even sampled their song “Here, There,
and Everywhere” on his track “White Ferrari.”

